{"operations":[{"content":"The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as established by the amendment adopted 2 May 2026. Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies. The bylaws state that the general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present, but this is superseded by the amendment.\n\n[[cite:obs-d0086e18845573f97c098e9c7e8d509c697a2f79 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]\n[[cite:obs-866f485db2e1ab744efb94a837890dc74426b27a \"The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present.\"]]","expected_sha256":"436a15c7e332c0d188ca4600961246fbd84f9499c7fef4c72f7d8c338d24b363","kind":"modify","path":"doc/quorum.md"}],"rationale":"Added the quorum definition from the 2 May 2026 amendment, stated that it overrides the bylaws quorum, and cited both sources exactly as required."}